          "In Part 2 of our Milestone Project, we build the core economic modeling component: the Statistical Arm's Length Range Simulator under Rule 10CA and Section 92C. When tax authorities challenge intra-group pricing, corporate taxpayers must produce statistically sound benchmarking distributions that withstand judicial scrutiny at the Income Tax Appellate Tribunal (ITAT).",
          "Our simulation engine takes a tested party's actual financial results\u2014operating revenue, total operating costs, and resulting operating margin (OP/TC or OP/OR)\u2014and benchmark it against a verified multi-year dataset of comparable uncontrolled companies. If the dataset contains six or more comparables, the engine constructs the statutory 35th-to-65th percentile range pursuant to Rule 10CA. If the dataset contains fewer than six entries, the engine automatically pivots to the arithmetic mean with a statutory 3% tolerance band.",
